# Topic rights per account; anything not granted is refused. Each service publishes exactly
# its own contract topics (the topic table in docs/architecture/overview.md) and reads
# exactly the topics it subscribes to, without wildcards: a topic added later gets no
# rights until it is added here. shared/runtime/tests/test_topics.py checks both against
# the code.

user physics-engine
topic write sensors/plant
topic write sensors/boiler
topic write sensors/turbine
topic write sensors/system/heartbeat
topic write status/physics-engine

user plc-controller
topic write alerts/warning
topic write alerts/critical
topic write alerts/snapshot
topic write plc/events
topic write status/plc-controller

user alert-manager
topic read alerts/warning
topic read alerts/critical
topic read alerts/snapshot
topic write alarms/changes

user historian
topic read sensors/plant
topic read sensors/boiler
topic read sensors/turbine
topic read alarms/changes
topic read plc/events
topic read status/physics-engine
topic read status/plc-controller

user api-gateway
topic read plc/events
topic read alarms/changes

user opcua-server
topic read sensors/plant
topic read sensors/boiler
topic read sensors/turbine
topic read alarms/changes

# The container healthcheck reads the broker's own statistics.
user monitor
topic read $SYS/#
